        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(skill-workshop): reject invalid proposal list limits",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`skill_workshop` proposal listing accepted malformed `limit` values by falling back to the default page size instead of reporting an input error. That made the runtime less strict than the tool schema and sibling list-style tools that require positive integer limits.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe list action now uses the shared positive-integer parameter reader for `limit`, preserving the existing default when the field is omitted and the existing upper-bound clamp for valid large limits.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMalformed list limits now fail fast with a clear validation error. Valid list calls, omitted limits, and existing proposal listing behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: current head `94035bc91222a1096a42efa482ddf7e92c3494f3` rejects malformed `skill_workshop` list limits while preserving omitted and valid list limits.\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` runtime proof from the repo root, importing `createSkillWorkshopTool`, creating two proposals in an isolated temp workspace, then executing real `skill_workshop` `action=list` calls.\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/skill-workshop-tool.test.ts`\n  - `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n- Observed result:\n  - Omitted limit: `action=list` succeeded and returned `count=2`.\n  - Valid limit: `action=list, limit=1` succeeded and returned `count=1`.\n  - Malformed limit: `action=list, limit=1.5` failed with `ToolInputError: limit must be a positive integer`.\n  - Focused Vitest passed: 1 file, 12 tests.\n  - Diff whitespace check passed.",
